    "name": "two values sent in one frame are both delivered, in order",
    "clauses": [
      "C2"
    ],
    "because": "C2 — inputs are queued per port and `update` shifts entries one at a time (node.ts :568-609); nothing collapses a queue to its newest entry after the first update. Two Increases in one frame send 1 then 2; the Value Changed downstream sees both and pulses twice; the Counter after it counts the pulses. A target that keeps only the newest value per turn reads 2 here, not 3.",
