  {
    "name": "an identical value sent again is delivered again — no equality short-circuit",
    "clauses": [
      "C2"
    ],
    "because": "C2 — `setInputValue` writes and invokes the setter unconditionally (node.ts :331-354). A Log passes its Value through and flags on every write (log.ts :120-129); a Switch's State setter announces EVERY write on Switched (switch.ts :64-68). `true` written twice in one frame reaches the Switch twice and Switched fires twice; the Counter counts them. A target that short-circuits identical writes counts one.",
    "nodes": {
      "a": {
        "type": "net.noodl.Log"
      },
      "s": {
        "type": "Switch"
      },
      "c": {
        "type": "Counter"
      }
    },
    "wires": [
